&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We seek an experienced, results-driven purchasing manager to join our team at Groww. As a purchase manager, you will be responsible for handling the procurement process, sourcing suppliers and managing vendor relationships to ensure a seamless supply chain and optimise costs. You will also collaborate with cross-functional teams, make strategic decisions and implement best practices within our procurement function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to our company&#39;s success and be part of a dynamic team in a competitive market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement procurement strategies and policies for cost optimization and supply chain efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, evaluate, and select suppliers based on quality, cost-effectiveness, and ethical standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate contracts and terms with suppliers to ensure favorable pricing and mutually beneficial agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage supplier relationships, including performance evaluation, issue resolution, and long-term partnership building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct market research and analysis to stay updated on industry trends and pricing fluctuations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor inventory levels, analyze demand patterns, and implement inventory management strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with internal stakeholders to understand requirements and align procurement with organizational goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement procurement systems and tools to streamline processes and enhance efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and present procurement reports, performance metrics, and cost-saving opportunities to management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with regulatory requirements and promote ethical and sustainable sourcing practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop procurement metrics to track performance and identify areas for improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Admin, HR, IT, and Marketing spends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred skills and qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in supply chain management, business administration, engineering or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years in procurement/purchasing in a fast-paced, competitive environment in the Indian market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of procurement principles, strategies and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong skills in budgeting, cost optimisation and negotiation techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of vendor management and inventory management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An analytical mind with excellent communication and interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work collaboratively with cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in using procurement software and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of local and national laws and regulations related to procurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work in a fast-paced and competitive environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Admin , HR, IT , Marketing Spends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
